  "review": [
    "Remove three synthetic card-instance compatibility unions: the eight-byte extension initializer overlay, the mode/unknown0x37 alias and the legacy upkeep-byte/token-keyword overlay. Preserve the actual four-byte native extension union, info-slot union and eot-toughness union.",
    "Restore native direct fields unused30, mode, unused0x124, unused0x128 and unused0x12a with their original widths and offsets. The only two token-keyword references become unused0x124 with the same uint32_t operations.",
    "Update the card-instance template aggregate initializer to those declarations. Every native load-time byte must remain identical; no algorithm statement or runtime assignment changes.",
    "Restore count_and_card_t::csvid to the original card_id_t enum. It remains at offset four in the eight-byte record; all eighteen table initializers and collation consumer statements stay untouched.",
    "Memorial ai remains unresolved: four call sites record one, Folly has no original value record, and the 2020 card file contains stubs. Do not invent an original argument.",
    "One combined build and focused current card/record checks follow. No full comparison or historical replay."
  ],
